    {
      "title": "Chapter 6: TCS and Putting It All Together",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "title": "Case Study: A Salaried Investor Tracks TDS Across Salary, FDs, Rent and a Flat Purchase",
          "slug": "case-study-a-salaried-investor-tracks-tds-across-salary-fds-rent-and-a-flat-purchase",
          "body": [
            {
              "_key": "c6l3-001",
              "_type": "bigIdea",
              "text": "One salaried person, one tax year, six different TDS provisions, two roles. Follow Rajeev through twelve months and every rule in this course falls into place."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c6l3-002",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c6l3-002s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Rajeev Menon, 38, is a product manager in Bengaluru earning ₹22,00,000 in tax year 2026-27. He keeps money in fixed deposits, holds a few dividend-paying shares, rents a flat at ₹65,000 a month, and in December he buys a flat of his own. By 31 March 2027 he has been a deductee six times over and a deductor twice. This final lesson walks through his year month by month, with every number checked.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c6l3-003",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c6l3-003s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Cast of Numbers",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
